    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "WPW with pre-excited AF:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if unstable, synchronized DC cardioversion; if stable, IV ibutilide, IV procainamide or synchronized cardioversion."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "IV dose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " loading infusion of 20 mg/mL at 1 mL/min for 25–30 min (500–600 mg; max 1 g total), then a maintenance infusion of 2–6 mg/min; hospital use with monitoring."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "During infusion:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " pause if BP falls ≥15 mm Hg; QRS widening >25% or marked QT prolongation suggests overdose, stop at a 50% increase; lower doses in renal impairment or age >50 (procainamide and NAPA accumulate); periodic CBC and ANA may be helpful."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " complete heart block (avoid in second-degree block or hemiblock without a pacemaker); established SLE; torsades de pointes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Serious ADRs:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " blood dyscrasias (0.5%), especially leukopenia or agranulocytosis, sometimes fatal; long-term use often gives a positive ANA, with or without a lupus-like syndrome."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " other class Ia drugs (quinidine, disopyramide) add conduction slowing, depressed contractility and hypotension."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
